🔹 Program 13: Virtual Destructor

📌 Description

This program demonstrates the importance of a virtual destructor in a polymorphic base class.

A "Derived" object is created dynamically and accessed using a "Base*" pointer.

When the pointer is deleted, the derived destructor executes first, followed by the base destructor.

🎯 Concept Used

Virtual Destructor and Safe Polymorphic Destruction

💡 Key Point

A polymorphic base class should generally have a virtual destructor so that derived objects are destroyed correctly through base pointers.
